{"ts":"2026-05-17T06:23:17.480Z","author":"claude-code-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-qa2h"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"auto-release.yml workflow_dispatch silently overrides explicit push=false to true"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-05-17 while dry-running auto-release after the close --reason fix. The workflow's ternary `${{ github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' && inputs.push || 'true' }}` evaluates as: when push=false, `&& false` short-circuits to `false`, then `|| 'true'` falls through to the cron default 'true'. Result: an operator can never run a true dry-run, because INPUT_PUSH stays 'true' and the workflow's own dry_run+push guard exits 2.\n\nFix shipped this session: nest a coercion ternary so `inputs.push && 'true' || 'false'` yields a string first, before the outer fallback runs. Same fix applied to dry_run and allow_same_day_release.\n\nCron path is unaffected (it never enters the workflow_dispatch branch), but operators can now dispatch with dry_run=true push=false to validate the pipeline without making a real release."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["auto-release","bug","ci","github-actions","pm-cli","release"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-05-17T06:23:17.480Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-05-17T06:23:17.480Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/assignee","value":"claude-code-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-code-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"cfb47ee840bdd6a1dba858d8f979071594d75d3f3fb835fd5470d73fe87ffffa","message":""}
